WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.709 --> 00:00:05.400
important question: how far would the
earth stretch if you cut it into one

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.590
meter cubes, just like in minecraft, and
lay them end to end in a long line

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:16.260
through space? Well as it happens there's
a giant Minecraft project underway to

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.470
recreate the entire Earth within the
game's universe at a one-to-one scale

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:25.800
but instead of asking them to
deconstruct this earth and lay it out

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.150
to answer this question, we can
just calculate it and let me tell you it

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:35.670
is way further than you might think.
And that's because volumes are super

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.329
underrated and this was something which
occurred to me when I was debating with

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:42.570
someone over the classic question of
whether it's ever okay to pee in a

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.719
swimming pool...
now who is arguing for which side isn't

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:49.500
important but basically one was claiming
that it's an atrocious thing to do

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.800
because then everyone's getting covered
in your pee and the other side simply

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.670
pointed out that it's not actually the
case because when you compare it to the

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:00.660
volume of water held in the average
swimming pool it becomes so insanely

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.100
diluted that it's basically negligible.
And so to settle this we ran the numbers

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.630
and based on a standard 25 metre pool
that is 10 meters wide and 1.3 meters

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:15.119
deep then that contains 325 cubic meters
of water and now compare this to the

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:19.470
average urination volume of I don't know
a 5 foot 5 50 kilogram female which

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.850
Google suggests is about 0.3 of a liter
and then compare the two and that equals

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:30.390
a ratio of over 1 million to 1. It's like
if you take one milliliter of orange

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:36.390
juice, and add it to 100
milliliters of water, shake that up, then

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:40.740
take one milliliter of that, add it to a
second hundred millilitres and then do

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:48.119
it a third time. I mean by this point
this is so diluted you could drink it,  let alone

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:52.350
worrying about having it on your skin. In
fact it's about as dangerous for you as

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:58.200
homeopathy is good for you because, by
the way, dilution is what homeopathy is

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.270
all - about the idea that the more dilute
a substance is the more of a positive

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:07.649
effect it has on your body and in fact
whenever you see one of those 30 C

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:11.670
labels on a bottle of homeopathy, what
that means is that they've done this

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:16.770
hundred to one dilution process 30 times
in a row, which corresponds to one part

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:21.510
in 10 to the 60. And means that you are
almost certainly without a shadow of a

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:26.430
doubt consuming exactly zero molecules
of whatever belladonna or arsenic you

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:32.030
think that you should be ingesting. But
anyway my point is is that volumes are

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.880
incredibly underrated and nothing
demonstrates this better than this

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.560
question of how far the Earth's volume
would stretch if you cut it into one

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.120
meter cubes and lay them out in a long
line through space. Now if you want to

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.319
pause and calculate it then go ahead, but
first what does your gut say? Do you

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:53.989
think you could stretch to the moon? how
about 150 million kilometers to the Sun?

00:02:53.989 --> 00:03:01.380
well the answer is it would stretch the
entire way across the Milky Way!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.920
I couldn't believe it myself but the earth
contains roughly as many cubic meters in

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:10.739
it as the diameter of our entire galaxy -
a galaxy that contains around 250

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:15.239
billion stars and is so big it takes
light - the fastest thing in the universe -

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:20.040
over a hundred thousand years to cross.
Just put that into perspective our

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.989
nearest star system, Alpha Centauri, is
only four light years away, but that's

00:03:24.989 --> 00:03:29.280
still a distance so vast that if the Sun
was a tennis ball in Los Angeles

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.739
Alpha Centauri would be another tennis
ball in Dallas Texas-  2,000 kilometers

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:38.400
away! And if you find this hard to wrap
your head around you're not alone

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.970
because all of our instincts really just
evolved to deal with linear

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.980
relationships, where things scan up in a
proximate proportion to one another but

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.420
because volume operates in three
dimensions, the ratio between it and the

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:55.530
length of the object scales up cubically, and cubic growth wasn't a

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:58.650
calculation we really needed to know
when we were running around on the

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:02.130
savanna.
what's even cooler is, the smaller the

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:06.390
size of cubes that you cut a volume up
into to lay out in a line, the further

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:11.100
that line stretches because there are
exponentially more of those cubes.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.150
In fact, there's a size of cube you could
cut the earth into so then it stretches

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:21.380
across the entire observable universe!
